CODE PROMPT 43 — Pool live updates (clock-reveal + leaderboard poll; NO postgres_changes)
Goal: make /pool feel live with no Realtime subscription. Two mechanisms, both on-read (no stored score table, no schema/migration, no postgres_changes): (1) a client-clock kickoff timer that refetches the gated read when a match crosses kickoff so others' picks reveal live; (2) a visibility-gated leaderboard poll so standings track results as matches resolve.
Decision record (lock it): no pool_pick subscription. pool_pick RLS SELECT is league-scoped and clock-less (anti-copying is in the server read query, not RLS — P40), so raw frames would leak pre-kickoff predictions; and revealable ⇒ past-kickoff ⇒ locked, so there are no live revealed-pick changes to show. Subscription = leak surface, no payoff. Leave the dormant P40 publication entry in place (out of scope to remove).
Staging: branch feat/pool-live off current main. Conventional commits, no force-push. Touch ONLY apps/web/app/pool/**, apps/web/src/pool/**, pool tests, pool-scoped css. NO schema/migration, NO shared files, NO nav edit, NO brain-file edits (report a docs delta for the post-merge commit).
1. Clock-reveal (PoolClient). Reuse P42's live clock. Derive the soonest future kickoffAt among matches whose others'-picks are still hidden; schedule one timer to that instant; on fire → refetch the gated read (the existing P42 path — router.refresh()/loader refetch) → re-derive the next timer. Server stays authoritative: the client clock only decides when to refetch; the server read re-applies the kickoff gate with server now and returns the correct revealed set (client drift only shifts timing by seconds; the poll is a backstop). Clear timers on unmount; never schedule past instants; coalesce shared instants.
2. Leaderboard visibility-poll. While the Leaderboard tab is active AND document is visible (Page Visibility API), refetch the existing on-read leaderboard loader on a 60s interval; refetch immediately on tab-activate and on visibilitychange→visible; pause/clear when the Picks tab is active or the doc is hidden. No new endpoint, no stored table.
3. Reveal-leak guard (headline invariant + test). The client reads other managers' predictions from nothing but the gated loader result — no raw pick payloads from any source, under any refetch path. Extend the P42 contract smoke to reaffirm this under the new clock/poll refetches.
4. Tests (Vitest, P37/P38 contract-smoke style, fake timers). Clock-reveal: timer scheduled to the next hidden-pick kickoff; firing triggers exactly one gated refetch and re-derives the next; no schedule for past/locked; cleared on unmount. Poll: fires only while leaderboard visible+active; immediate refetch on activate/visible; paused on hidden/Picks-tab. Leak guard as above. Report test-count delta.
